# Environment variables — EVERY variant, including operator backups.
#
# This used to be `.env` / `.env.local` / `**/.env` only, which matched the live files and
# nothing else. Operators DO copy an env file aside before a cutover, and those copies were
# untracked but NOT ignored: on 2026-07-26 `./.env.bak-pre-042c477` held the CURRENT
# production SEARXNG_SECRET in plaintext and `app/.env.bak-pre-v4flash` held the retired
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL value that broke both pools for a day. This repo is PUBLIC, and it already
# has one `git add -A` contamination on record (af65e40), so "untracked" was one careless
# stage away from a real leak. The secret was never actually committed — verified with
# `git log --all -S<secret>` — so the hole was closed rather than a rotation performed.
#
# Keep the negations narrow: `*.example` files are TRACKED on purpose, and PR #8 exists
# because one of them once carried a real-looking 64-hex secret. See
# tests/test_env_files_cannot_be_committed.py, which fails if this block is narrowed again.
.env*
**/.env*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Logs
*.log

# Model files (large)
*.safetensors
*.bin
!requirements.txt

# Scraped property cache (regenerable via build_scraped_dataset.py)
app/data/scraped_property_listings.csv

# Playwright MCP artifacts
.playwright-mcp/
chroma_db_agent_memory/
app/chroma_db_agent_memory/

# Refactor implementation plan (local only)
REFACTOR_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

# Packaging and persistent runtime cache
/build/
/dist/
/src/*.egg-info/
.runtime/
# ...and every sibling variant — the SAME hole as the env block above, different artifact.
# `.runtime/` with a trailing slash matches that one directory and nothing else, so the
# per-experiment trees an operator actually creates — `.runtime-fpon/`, `.runtime-fpoff/`,
# `.runtime-hardening/`, `.runtime-legctl/`, `.runtime-fccontrol/`, `.runtime-fccompact/`,
# all six of which are sitting untracked in the production tree right now — matched no rule.
#
# This is the class whose INSTANCE is already patched further down as
# `/evaluation/results/schema_compaction_ab_2026-07-22/`: commit af65e40 is a `git add -A`
# twin of 994be81 that swept a 3469-line untracked results package in, and the response was
# to name that one directory. Naming instances is how this repo reached seven of one defect
# class; HANDOFF §0 says only a guard stops the eighth.
#
# Evidence packages are retained on disk and deliberately NEVER committed (HANDOFF §6).
# Scoped to `.runtime*` on purpose: `evaluation/results/<package>/` trees such as
# `live_routed_98` and `phase2_ab_2026-07-19` ARE committed provenance and must stay tracked.
.runtime-*/
.runtime*.jsonl
*.sqlite3

# SearXNG live config: a runtime file the container mounts and chowns to its own
# uid. Tracking it causes git-vs-container ownership conflicts, so it's ignored;
# bootstrap from deploy/searxng-settings.yml.example (deploy/update.sh does this).
/searxng/settings.yml

# Local user credential store (password HASHES — never commit, even by mistake).
# Default lives under .runtime/ (already ignored) but pin the filename anywhere it lands.
users.json
**/users.json
users.json.tmp
**/users.json.tmp

# Untracked junk archive (moved-aside legacy files)
archive/

